alizers to these, accessing an uninitialized bool can get /weird/"],["c66dc7f5_a46c5674",14,0,0,"I guess you'll be sending these to browser, which will then CDP-encode them?"],["dc95b142_a282c332",17,0,1,"(Probably want const-refs here, too)"]],0,457],[7303611,20452,396,8.956,7.286,[[2,0.502,49,198],[23,0.485,1,194],[22,0.012,2,4]],[["0b7399ae_b2ecfcfc",18,-1,1,"Same here"],["12f4b32f_f57d5f88",16,-1,1,"nit: Comments for the fields?"],["c0d21c4f_e71956ae",18,-1,1,"nit: You could also and these directly: return data.ReadRuleType(&out->rule_type) && data.ReadHostPattern(&out->host_pattern) ..."],["89ebc7e6_e1eda75b",19,0,0,"(Likewise for copyability)."],["8c2763d0_c2408eab",20,0,1,"This probably should stay as a value since you're passing a temporary to it? (So it ends up as a copy vs. move thing)."],["be951322_cfddb12f",19,0,1,"Going for const-ref + copy might be slightly cheaper than the copy + move you're doing, because std::string is kinda huge to enable inline short strings?"],["cf52a6c2_3732c47a",20,0,1,"Likewise, please initialize the bools (enums probably too; come to think of it, but I am not sure of what the language says about out-of-range values, they may be safe for anything in the underlying…"],["f3702385_fad538c1",20,0,0,"Likewise here --- may be able to make this move-only."]],0,458]]}